      "panel-map": {
        "kind": "Panel",
        "spec": {
          "data": {
            "kind": "QueryGroup",
            "spec": {
              "queries": [
                {
                  "kind": "PanelQuery",
                  "spec": {
                    "hidden": false,
                    "query": {
                      "datasource": {
                        "name": "duckdb"
                      },
                      "group": "motherduck-duckdb-datasource",
                      "kind": "DataQuery",
                      "spec": {
                        "editorMode": "code",
                        "format": 1,
                        "rawQuery": true,
                        "rawSql": "-- Cuenca as CityJSON tiles (datasets/cuenca-3d/tiles.py): the city cut into cells of about 550 m, each\n-- building in the cell of its middle, one file per cell with its roof and wall faces and each face's\n-- colour as a CityJSON material. One row per tile: the URL the browser fetches it from (the gateway\n-- serves the dataset's cityjson/ folder at /datasets/cuenca-3d/cityjson/) and the box its buildings\n-- cover. The City Model layer reads only the tiles in view, the nearest the middle first; from afar,\n-- OpenStreetMap's blocks.\nSELECT '${site:raw}/datasets/cuenca-3d/cityjson/' || file AS city_url, west, south, east, north, buildings\nFROM 'http://feeds/datasets/cuenca-3d/tiles.parquet'\nORDER BY file"
                      },
                      "version": "v0"
                    },
                    "refId": "A"
                  }
                }
              ],
              "queryOptions": {},
              "transformations": []
            }
          },
          "description": "Every building of Cuenca (those in the map's view): its footprint from Overture Maps, its height from OpenStreetMap where someone measured it and from its measured neighbours where not, and its roof coloured by the satellite pixels over it (Sentinel-2, 12 September 2024, 10 m), hipped where they are clay tile; the centre's churches and the Corte Provincial de Justicia drawn from a description of each. Walls take a colour from the roof's kind, a rule, not data. The sun stands where it does at 10:00 on that day. Hover a surface for its building's facts.",
